The IPI module is used to send/receive user data between multiple e200 cores of Geul.
This uses the FreeRTOS features of Events and Queues to transfer the data between multiple cores.
An interrupt is generated as soon as there is some data to be received 
on a pariticular core.

1. The IPI driver API:

1)
enum IPIEventID {
	IPI_EVT_ID_NULL = -1,
	IPI_EVT_ID0 = 0,
	IPI_EVT_ID1 = 1,
	IPI_EVT_ID2 = 2,
	IPI_EVT_ID3 = 3,
	IPI_EVT_ID4 = 4,
	IPI_EVT_ID5 = 5,
	IPI_EVT_ID6 = 6,
	IPI_EVT_ID7 = 7,
	IPI_EVT_ID8 = 8,
	IPI_EVT_ID9 = 9,
	IPI_EVT_ID10 = 10,
	IPI_EVT_ID11 = 11,
	IPI_EVT_ID12 = 12,
	IPI_EVT_ID13 = 13,
	IPI_EVT_ID14 = 14,
	IPI_EVT_ID15 = 15,
	IPI_EVT_ID_MAX = 16
};

Description:
	IPI Event ID is used to wake up the target task which will be notified.
	This Event ID is local ID on each e200 Core.
	Each Event ID is associated to one FreeRTOS queue.

2)
enum IPIEventID vIPIEventRegister(enum IPIEventID eventID, QueueHandle_t *Queue);

Description:
	Register IPI Event ID for the FreeRTOS task which will be notified by remote or local task.

Parameter:
	enum IPIEventID eventID:
	User can specify the event ID which has not been acquired on this core.
	User can also pass IPI_EVT_ID_NULL parameter and this function will allocate one event ID for user in success.

	QueueHandle_t *Queue:
	User should pass one point of FreeRTOS Queue to this function.
	The function will set this point with one FreeRTOS Queue associated to the event ID returened in success.

Return:
	enum IPIEventID:
	If user specifies the event ID which has not been registered,
	the return value is just the event ID passed, otherwise, the return value is IPI_EVT_ID_NULL.
	If the parameter enum IPIEventID eventID is IPI_EVT_ID_NULL,
	the return value is one of value from IPI_EVT_ID0 to IPI_EVT_ID15 in success or IPI_EVT_ID_NULL in failure.

3)
void vIPIEventUnRegister(enum IPIEventID eventID);

Description:
        Un-Register the IPI Event ID whhich could be used by other local task later.

4)
void vIPICoreInit(void);

Description:
	Initialize IPI communication context on each core.
	This function should be called on each core after MPIC initalization and before tasks are created.
	This function creates one IPI peer task to receive event from IPI ISRs and send data to APP tasks.
	This function registers/enables 4 IPI interrupts for 4 IPI RX channels respectively.
	Each IPI RX channel is associated to one remote core or local core to receive data.
	Only one IPI TX channel is associated to local core.

5)
BaseType_t vIPISendData(u8 dstCore, enum IPIEventID eventID, void *useData);

Description:
	Send point of user Data to the target task on remote/local core with its event ID registered.
Parmaeters:
	u8 dstCore:
	Target core ID (0~3).
	
	enum IPIEventID eventID:
	IPI event ID registered by target task.

	void *useData:
	Point of user data which will be sent to the target task.

Return:
	BaseType_t:
	pdTRUE in success.
	pdFALSE in fail (queue full).

6)
void vIPIGlobalQStatusCheck(int dstCore, int srcCore);

Description:
	Debug purpose to check the status of global queues.

7)
void vIPISyncSet(void);

Description:
	Called after EVENT IDs are registered. Used to notify remote task that receiver is ready.

8)
int vIPISyncCheck(void);

Description:
	Check if remote tasks are ready to receive data.

Return:
	pdTRUE, remote tasks are ready to receive data.
	pdFALSE, remote tasks have not registered event ID to receive data.



2. Demo code for reference:

1)
void vGeulIPIDemo(void);

Description:
	Entry of the demo, which creates on task to test.

2)
Test scenarios:
	i)  Send data from multiple cores to single core concurrent.
	user needs to set gIPITestMode to IPI_MULTI_SRC_SINGLE_DST for this scenario.

	ii) Send data from single core to multiple cores.
	user needs to set gIPITestMode to IPI_SINGLE_SRC_MULTI_DST for this scenario.

	iii)Send data to its right neighbor core and receive data from its left neighbor core.

		core0->core1->core2->core3--
		^                           |
 		|___________________________|

	user needs to set gIPITestMode to IPI_CHAIN_SINGLE_SRC_SINGLE_DST for this scenario.

	The test code will quit if all the expected data are sent and received.
	To make sure the connections are stable and reliable.

3) Pseudocode to creae simple IPI communication between two coree.
This will transmit and receive a single piece of data(an int)
between between 0<-->1 and 2<-->3

static void vGeulIPIDemoTest(void *pvParam)
{
        enum IPIEventID eventID=IPI_EVT_ID1;
        u32 current_core = ulMpicCurrentCore();
        QueueHandle_t rxQueue;
        QueueHandle_t rxQueueAvailable;
        QueueSetHandle_t rxQueueSet = xQueueCreateSet(IPI_DEMO_EVENT_NUM * 8);  //Add maximum 8 elements per queue
        vIPIEventRegister(eventID, &rxQueue);
        xQueueAddToSet(rxQueue, rxQueueSet);
        int txData=10;
        int txData2=12;
        void *rxData=NULL;
        int ret;
        vIPISyncSet();
        while (1) {
                if (vIPISyncCheck() > 0)
                        break;
                vTaskDelay(1);
        }
        while(1)
        {
                rxData=NULL;
                if(current_core == 0)
                {
                        txData=txData+1;
                        log_info("Send to core 1 data=%d\r\n", txData);
                        if(pdFALSE == vIPISendData(1, eventID, (void *)txData))
                                log_info("\nIPISendData fail");
                }
                else if(current_core == 1)
                {
                        txData=txData+10;
                        log_info("Send to core 0 data=%d\r\n", txData);
                        if(pdFALSE == vIPISendData(0, eventID, (void *)txData))
                                log_info("\nIPISendData fail");
                }
                else if(current_core == 2)
                {
                        txData2=txData2+11;
                        log_info("Send to core 3 data=%d\r\n", txData2);
                        if(pdFALSE == vIPISendData(3, eventID, (void *)txData2))
                                log_info("\nIPISendData fail");

                }
                else if(current_core == 3)
                {
                        txData2=txData2+10;
                        log_info("Send to core 2 data=%d\r\n", txData2);
                        if(pdFALSE == vIPISendData(2, eventID, (void *)txData2))
                                log_info("\nIPISendData fail");
                }
                vTaskDelay(1);
                rxQueueAvailable = (QueueHandle_t)xQueueSelectFromSet(rxQueueSet, 1);
                if(rxQueueAvailable)
                {
                        ret = xQueueReceive(rxQueueAvailable, &rxData, 0);
                        if(ret==pdTRUE)						
                        {
                                log_info("\n\rData received=%d",(int )rxData);
                        }
                }
                else
                {
                        log_info("\n\r rxQueue not Availaible");

                }
        }
}
